WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.742
On this slide, we are focusing on return and error handling.

00:00:03.742 --> 00:00:08.187
Start with the meaning of the idea before worrying about the exact syntax.

00:00:08.187 --> 00:00:16.892
Ask what information is going in, what Python is doing with it, and what result should come out.

00:00:16.892 --> 00:00:20.362
Return sends a value back to the program so later code can store it, combine it, test it,

00:00:20.362 --> 00:00:22.647
or pass it into another function.

00:00:22.647 --> 00:00:26.677
Print only displays a value.

00:00:26.677 --> 00:00:28.182
Before clicking Run, predict the output.

00:00:28.182 --> 00:00:34.332
Then run the cell, inspect the result, and change one value or condition at a time.

00:00:34.332 --> 00:00:37.672
Rerun it and explain why the output changed.

00:00:37.672 --> 00:00:42.687
The goal is to understand the relationship between input, process, and output.
